      {
        "num": "9",
        "name": "Exercise 94",
        "exercises": [
          {
            "label": "Exercise 94 (Chapter 12) — from the book. (Miscellaneous) Combine each set of sentences into one Simple sentence. (Key partly legible; some answers worked from the rules.)",
            "items": [
              {
                "q": "1. Homer was a great poet. He was born somewhere. Nobody knows where.",
                "a": "Homer, the great poet, was born at a place nobody knows."
              },
              {
                "q": "2. He was a leader. He did not follow other men. Such was his nature.",
                "a": "He was a leader by nature, not a follower of other men."
              },
              {
                "q": "3. I bought this hat two years ago. It is still good. It is fit to wear.",
                "a": "This hat, bought two years ago, is still good and fit to wear."
              },
              {
                "q": "4. He devoted himself to public affairs. He never took a holiday. This continued for thirty years.",
                "a": "For thirty years he devoted himself to public affairs without taking a holiday."
              },
              {
                "q": "5. Clive made proposals. Some opposed the proposals. The majority supported them. They were carried.",
                "a": "Clive's proposals, opposed by some and supported by the majority, were carried."
              },
              {
                "q": "6. Clive was determined to reform the administration. Reforms were needed. He informed the council accordingly.",
                "a": "Determined to reform the administration, which needed reforms, Clive informed the council accordingly."
              },
              {
                "q": "7. The man was innocent. He could have defended himself. He refused to speak. He was afraid of convicting his friend.",
                "a": "Though innocent and able to defend himself, he refused to speak for fear of convicting his friend."
              },
              {
                "q": "8. He was in prison. His friend was in the next cell. There was a brick wall between the cells. He made a hole in the wall. He was able to talk to his friend.",
                "a": "He was in prison, his friend in the next cell, with only a brick wall between them; making a hole in the wall, he was able to talk to his friend."
              },
              {
                "q": "9. The boy was drowning. He shouted for help. A workman heard the boy's shouts. He plunged into the river. He risked his own life.",
                "a": "Hearing the drowning boy's shouts for help, a workman plunged into the river at the risk of his own life."
              },
              {
                "q": "10. The traveller was toiling slowly over the desert. He suddenly turned round. He heard his companion's voice. His companion was crying for help.",
                "a": "Toiling slowly over the desert, the traveller suddenly turned round on hearing his companion crying for help."
              },
              {
                "q": "11. We returned down the valley of the Jumna. We came first to Delhi. Delhi is the capital of India.",
                "a": "Returning down the valley of the Jumna, we came first to Delhi, the capital of India."
              },
              {
                "q": "12. The art of printing was introduced into England during the reign of Edward IV. The art of printing was introduced by William Caxton. William Caxton was a native of Kent.",
                "a": "The art of printing was introduced into England by William Caxton, a native of Kent, during the reign of Edward IV."
              },
              {
                "q": "13. He struck his foot against a stone. He fell to the ground. He made his clothes very dirty.",
                "a": "Having struck his foot against a stone, he fell to the ground and made his clothes very dirty."
              },
              {
                "q": "14. The sun shone on the corn. The corn ripened. It did this in a short time. The farmer was filled with joy.",
                "a": "The sun having shone on the corn and ripened it in a short time, the farmer was filled with joy."
              },
              {
                "q": "15. He opened his letters. He read them carefully. He sent for his clerk. He dictated answers to them.",
                "a": "Having opened and read his letters carefully, he sent for his clerk and dictated answers to them."
              },
              {
                "q": "16. He paid all his late father's debts. This was a very honest proceeding. It was very creditable to him.",
                "a": "His paying all his late father's debts was a very honest and creditable proceeding."
              },
              {
                "q": "17. He has two horses. He must feed them. He must water them. He must groom them. He must bring them to his master at 12 o'clock.",
                "a": "He has two horses to feed, water, groom and bring to his master at 12 o'clock."
              },
              {
                "q": "18. He goes to school. He wishes to learn. He wants to grow up honest, healthy and clever.",
                "a": "He goes to school to learn and to grow up honest, healthy and clever."
              },
              {
                "q": "19. There was a man hiding in my garden. He was armed with a gun. He was a Pathan. My notice was drawn to it.",
                "a": "My notice was drawn to a Pathan, armed with a gun, hiding in my garden."
              },
              {
                "q": "20. The soldiers were starving. Their ammunition was expended. Their clothes were in rags. Their leaders were dead. The enemy easily defeated them.",
                "a": "Starving, with their ammunition expended, their clothes in rags and their leaders dead, the soldiers were easily defeated by the enemy."
              },
              {
                "q": "21. Napoleon was the first Emperor of the French. He was a great soldier. He inspired his armies with the most war-like spirit. This was the cause of their many victories.",
                "a": "Napoleon, the first Emperor of the French and a great soldier, inspired his armies with the most war-like spirit, the cause of their many victories."
              },
              {
                "q": "22. Wellington was the greatest of English admirals. Napoleon was the greatest of French soldiers. They were contemporaries. They were the heroes of their respective countries.",
                "a": "Wellington, the greatest of English admirals, and Napoleon, the greatest of French soldiers, were contemporaries and the heroes of their respective countries."
              },
              {
                "q": "23. The miser laughed. He found himself to be richer by a rupee. He saw his adversary outwitted.",
                "a": "Finding himself richer by a rupee and seeing his adversary outwitted, the miser laughed."
              },
              {
                "q": "24. He hardened his heart. He wished to punish the people mercilessly. He wanted to make an example of them once and for all.",
                "a": "He hardened his heart to punish the people mercilessly and make an example of them once and for all."
              },
              {
                "q": "25. He receives much gratitude. He performs kindly actions. He is not harsh in the execution of his duty. He does not oppress the poor.",
                "a": "He receives much gratitude for his kindly actions, not being harsh in the execution of his duty or oppressing the poor."
              },
              {
                "q": "26. His friends assembled. They offered him their congratulations upon his safe return. Everybody was comfortably seated. He described all his adventures.",
                "a": "His friends having assembled and offered him their congratulations upon his safe return, and everybody being comfortably seated, he described all his adventures."
              },
              {
                "q": "27. The thieves poisoned the dog. He had brought it from England. He had trained it carefully to protect his property.",
                "a": "The thieves poisoned the dog he had brought from England and trained carefully to protect his property."
              },
              {
                "q": "28. Vultures appeared one after another. They were wheeling round and round. They were descending towards the spot. They had cruel beaks and talons.",
                "a": "Vultures, with cruel beaks and talons, appeared one after another, wheeling round and round and descending towards the spot."
              },
              {
                "q": "29. The room was covered with blood. It stained the walls and ceiling. It darkened the floor. It flowed in a stream under the door. It stood in puddles everywhere.",
                "a": "The room was covered with blood which stained the walls and ceiling, darkened the floor, flowed in a stream under the door and stood in puddles everywhere."
              },
              {
                "q": "30. The house had been pulled down. Another had been built in its place. It was difficult to identify the exact spot.",
                "a": "The house having been pulled down and another built in its place, it was difficult to identify the exact spot."
              },
              {
                "q": "31. He earned the hatred of all good men. He incited youths to crime. He furnished them with means. He himself kept safely out of the way in time of danger.",
                "a": "He earned the hatred of all good men by inciting youths to crime and furnishing them with means, while keeping himself safely out of the way in time of danger."
              },
              {
                "q": "32. He copied from the next boy. This was a mean and dishonest action. It brought disgrace upon him. He was punished for it.",
                "a": "Having copied from the next boy, a mean and dishonest action which brought disgrace upon him, he was punished for it."
              },
              {
                "q": "33. He had not sufficient courage. He could not face the opposition of his caste fellows. He could not go away from his native place to begin life afresh.",
                "a": "Lacking sufficient courage to face the opposition of his caste fellows, he could not go away from his native place to begin life afresh."
              },
              {
                "q": "34. Rabindranath Tagore founded Shantiniketan. He was a Nobel laureate. He was the author of the national anthem.",
                "a": "Rabindranath Tagore, a Nobel laureate and the author of the national anthem, founded Shantiniketan."
              },
              {
                "q": "35. He could not finish his work. He had no opportunity. He could not do much of it in fact. He was very often ill. He was frequently absent.",
                "a": "Being very often ill and frequently absent, he had no opportunity to finish his work and could not do much of it in fact."
              },
              {
                "q": "36. The criminal was a man of his own caste. He was an ungrateful and incorrigible wretch. He had often helped him.",
                "a": "The criminal, a man of his own caste and an ungrateful and incorrigible wretch, had often been helped by him."
              },
              {
                "q": "37. He went for a walk one day. He saw a wounded bird. He picked it up. He brought it home. He carefully tended it for some time. It completely recovered. This gave him great joy.",
                "a": "Going for a walk one day, he saw a wounded bird, picked it up, brought it home and tended it carefully for some time till it completely recovered, to his great joy."
              },
              {
                "q": "38. I knew a boy at school. He is now famous as a soldier. He is known to the tribesmen as the 'Sleepless One'. He is greatly feared by them.",
                "a": "I knew a boy at school who is now famous as a soldier, known to the tribesmen as the 'Sleepless One' and greatly feared by them."
              },
              {
                "q": "39. The water had boiled. The tea was made. The food was ready. The table was spread. They sat down to eat and drink.",
                "a": "The water having boiled, the tea made, the food ready and the table spread, they sat down to eat and drink."
              },
              {
                "q": "40. He deserves my thanks. He found my purse. He returned it to me. He took nothing out of it.",
                "a": "He deserves my thanks for having found my purse and returned it to me without taking anything out of it."
              },
              {
                "q": "41. I saw a dog. It had three legs. It had only one ear. It was a terrier. It was a well-bred little animal.",
                "a": "I saw a well-bred little terrier with three legs and only one ear."
              },
              {
                "q": "42. He must clean all the silver. He must put it away. He must lock it up. He must bring me the key of the box. These were my orders to him.",
                "a": "My orders to him were to clean all the silver, put it away, lock it up and bring me the key of the box."
              },
              {
                "q": "43. The horse had many of the points of a racer. It had slim legs. It had high withers. It had powerful quarters. It had a tremendous stride.",
                "a": "The horse, with slim legs, high withers, powerful quarters and a tremendous stride, had many of the points of a racer."
              },
              {
                "q": "44. He was a great statesman. He had worked well for his country. He was very popular. He was awarded the title of 'Bharat Ratna'.",
                "a": "He was a great statesman who had worked well for his country, was very popular and was awarded the title of 'Bharat Ratna'."
              },
              {
                "q": "45. Wood was collected. Camp fires were lighted. Food was cooked. Food was eaten. The army lay down to sleep.",
                "a": "Wood having been collected, camp fires lighted and food cooked and eaten, the army lay down to sleep."
              },
              {
                "q": "46. He alienated his friends. His conduct was disgraceful. He was put in gaol.",
                "a": "His disgraceful conduct alienated his friends, and he was put in gaol."
              },
              {
                "q": "47. Rama had a wide knowledge of the business. Krishna had the necessary capital. They combined resources. They entered into partnership.",
                "a": "Rama, with his wide knowledge of the business, and Krishna, with the necessary capital, combined resources and entered into partnership."
              },
              {
                "q": "48. Their father had a large sum of money. He divided it equally between them by his will. The daughters were eagerly sought in marriage.",
                "a": "Their father, by his will, divided a large sum of money equally between his daughters, who were eagerly sought in marriage."
              },
              {
                "q": "49. The ground is soft and marshy. There are many frogs. Snakes abound there. They are the enemies of mankind.",
                "a": "The ground being soft and marshy, with many frogs, snakes, the enemies of mankind, abound there."
              },
              {
                "q": "50. His hopes are high. His superiors are pleased with him. He is justified in hoping.",
                "a": "With high hopes and his superiors pleased with him, he is justified in hoping."
              },
              {
                "q": "51. He rode along for hours. He did not strike his horse. He did not spur it.",
                "a": "He rode along for hours without striking or spurring his horse."
              },
              {
                "q": "52. I have some advice. I must give it to you. I must impress it strongly upon you.",
                "a": "I have some advice to give you and to impress strongly upon you."
              },
              {
                "q": "53. I hear rumours about Laxman. He is an old pupil of mine. He is a good cricketer. He is a good football player. He is not a steady worker.",
                "a": "I hear rumours about Laxman, an old pupil of mine, a good cricketer and a good football player, but not a steady worker."
              },
              {
                "q": "54. He was delighted with the intelligence and brightness of the scholars. He overlooked the fact of their knowing few things by heart.",
                "a": "Delighted with the intelligence and brightness of the scholars, he overlooked their knowing few things by heart."
              },
              {
                "q": "55. He built a house. It had many large doors. It had many large windows. It had wide verandahs. It had a general air of coolness and comfort.",
                "a": "He built a house with many large doors, many large windows and wide verandahs, having a general air of coolness and comfort."
              },
              {
                "q": "56. He told a story. It was about a man. The man had great strength. He was a famous warrior.",
                "a": "He told a story about a man of great strength, a famous warrior."
              },
              {
                "q": "57. He came to Mumbai. He wished to see his father. He had some business to settle.",
                "a": "He came to Mumbai to see his father and to settle some business."
              },
              {
                "q": "58. After the storm the boat had no mast. It could not keep before the wind. It could not return to port.",
                "a": "After the storm the boat, having no mast, could neither keep before the wind nor return to port."
              },
              {
                "q": "59. The cage contains a tiger. The cage was strongly built. It was so built for this purpose.",
                "a": "The cage, strongly built for this purpose, contains a tiger."
              },
              {
                "q": "60. The ancient myths of India have been preserved in the minds of the people. They have been preserved with great care. This has been done by priests. It has also been done by the learned men. These are the guardians of the lamp of learning.",
                "a": "The ancient myths of India have been preserved with great care in the minds of the people by priests and learned men, the guardians of the lamp of learning."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
