                "q": "What is the substance of the poem 'Daffodils'?",
                "a": "As the poet was taking a solitary walk beside a lake one bright and breezy Spring morning, he suddenly came upon thousands and thousands of yellow daffodils under the trees beside the sparkling waters of the lake, 'Fluttering and dancing in the breeze'. The sight filled him with pleasure; but he did not know at the time all that the experience had added to his life. Many times afterwards, memory brought back that beautiful scene as a mental picture, which gave him over and over again the same sense of gladness."
